From 2a02e0d92de738a84ddff40822a34c4e7f5ea118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:43:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep debug-only declarations out of release targets

Gate analytics capture imports, app-server test-hook declarations, and CLI
update-test helpers with the same debug_assertions condition as their uses.
Retain the library and cloud-task fixes and extend the maintained regression
recipe to cover all targets in the five affected packages.

Fixes https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/29872
Base: rust-v0.162.1 (092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d)

Red: the expanded just check-release-warnings exits 101 for the analytics
capture imports. Hosted Linux release verification also reports unused
app-server hook declarations and CLI update-test helpers under -D warnings.
Green: the expanded recipe passes with local stable Rust 1.99.0 on the full
queue; maintained just fmt-check passes. Emitted patch verification is
recorded separately in release-debug-items-verification.json.
---
 codex-rs/analytics/src/client_tests.rs | 2 ++
 codex-rs/app-server/src/lib.rs         | 5 ++++-
 codex-rs/app-server/src/main.rs        | 3 +++
 codex-rs/cli/tests/update.rs           | 5 +++++
 codex-rs/cloud-tasks/src/lib.rs        | 2 ++
 justfile                               | 4 ++++
 6 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

